Z||000000||Ironhorse||08-03-2000||02:01 AM||||Hello to you all.  I have done some modification to my oil dipstick cuz I removed one of the bracket that it bolt up to.  Well when the engine was out of F-15, it looks doable.  Well when I put it in F-15, It's in the way where the battery is.  My father has a 90 Lumina 3.1 engine with a oil dipstick that goes straight up the engine instead at the angle of the enigne which is what 2.8 Fiero have.  I really really really want to install a 1990 Chev Lumina 3.1 oil dipstick into my `85 Fiero.  Is this possible as a straight out replacement or do you foresee a custom work involves?  Thanks for any information.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-03-2000||09:13 PM||||First thing you need to know is iff the new stick it the right lenght into the motor.<P>you need both sticks and tubes out. push the stick fully into the tube. make sure the distance from the shoulder on the block end of the tube to the tip of the stick is the same. Otherwise the rest of the stick and tube can be any length and you can mount it any way you want.||||reg||1
